{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RxioTRBp8HoW87kWgzejDA","type":"tool_result","content":"bugs:\n  - bug_id: BUG-2026-09-26T142500\n    date: \"2026-09-26\"\n    title: \"Pausing a stopped change erases its stop, and a resume can no longer lift it\"\n    severity: medium\n    priority: p2\n    scope: domain\n    what_happened: >\n      A change blocked on a stop a resume lifts (a stalled specification, an execution error) accepted\n      `/495 pause`. On resume it came back `blocked` with no stop reason, no detail and no longer\n      retryable: a second resume lifted nothing, the names of the lost answers were gone, and cancel\n      was the only way out left.\n    what_expected: >\n      A stopped change keeps its stop, its detail and its ways out whatever the operator does before\n      lifting it.\n    steps_to_reproduce:\n      - \"Take a change to the stop before G0 of a specification that no longer progresses.\"\n      - \"Run `/495 pause`, then `/495 resume` twice.\"\n      - \"The change stays `blocked` with `stop_reason` null and `stop_retryable` false, and `advance` writes nothing.\"\n    root_cause: >\n      `changePause` (`src/domain/change/decide.ts`) accepted any active change, blocked ones included.\n      It saved only the status in the resume point, and its `status.changed` event cleared the stop\n      reason, detail and retryability. `changeResume` restored `blocked` without them, and\n      `harness.resume` lifts a block only when its reason is `execution_error` or it is retryable. The\n      same code is on main for every stop a resume lifts; a stalled specification relies on that\n      resume for its recourse.\n    evidence: >\n      test/v0/change-rules.test.ts, \"refuses to pause a blocked change, which keeps its stop, its detail\n      and its retryability\", and test/v2/specification-reopening.test.ts, \"refuses to pause a stopped\n      change, whose stop a resume still lifts into a rewriting (6a)\": red at 0d67f46 (2 failures out\n      of 59, the pause accepted), green at 6d5a3e3, both in a detached worktree. Preflight green under\n      Node 26.9.0, 486 tests.\n    reopened: >\n      The guard `6d5a3e3` added to `changePause` left a second way in: a change blocked while an\n      intervention still ran. A `DomainError` thrown between `intervention.start` and\n      `intervention.finish` (a missing adopted artifact, a failed store write, a worker that does not\n      start) blocked the change and left the intervention `running`. `harness.pause` finishes a running\n      intervention before it commits `change.pause`, and `intervention.finished` sets the status to\n      `ready`: the guard saw a ready change, accepted the pause, and the stop was erased. The kernel now\n      ends the running intervention in `block`, in the same decision as the stop, so a blocked change\n    severity: medium\n    priority: p3\n    scope: adapters\n    what_happened: >\n      The integrator copies every changed path of the candidate into the project, then runs\n      `git add -A -- <selected paths>`. When one of those paths is matched by the project's `.gitignore`,\n      git prints \"The following paths are ignored by one of your .gitignore files\" and exits 1. The call\n      is not allowed to fail, so the integration falls into its `catch` and ends `uncertain`, which asks\n      the owner to investigate an accepted change whose files are all in place.\n    what_expected: >\n      A path git ignores is copied with the rest and left out of the commit; the change is integrated.\n    steps_to_reproduce:\n      - \"In a git project whose `.gitignore` lists `coverage/`, accept a candidate that adds `coverage/report.txt` and another tracked file.\"\n      - \"Accept the local integration.\"\n      - \"The integration ends `uncertain` and the commit is not made.\"\n    root_cause: >\n      `Integrator` (`src/adapters/git/integrator.ts`) calls `git(project, [\"add\", \"-A\", \"--\", ...selected_paths])`\n      without `allowFailure`, and the workspace walk that builds `selected_paths` does not read `.gitignore`.\n      Not introduced by a branch: the same code is on main.\n    evidence: >\n      Read on 2026-09-30, and git measured: `git add -A -- package.json node_modules/x/i.js` in a project\n      ignoring `node_modules/` prints the message above and exits 1, while the tracked file is still\n      staged. In a project that does not ignore `node_modules/`, the same command stages the dependency\n      files, which would commit them. The path from the integrator to that call was not run end to end.\n    risk_level: low\n    follow_ups: >\n      Stage only the paths git can index and never a `node_modules/` path, after copying every path the\n      candidate holds; a test on a project that ignores a candidate path, and on one that does not ignore\n      `node_modules/`.\n    status: open","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"dc0fdf1f-fc2c-45aa-b758-cfb626439464","uuid":"c84581f4-9311-4974-968d-d5e2fdb033cf","timestamp":"2026-09-30T01:15:50.414Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"bugs:\n  - bug_id: BUG-2026-09-26T142500\n    date: \"2026-09-26\"\n    title: \"Pausing a stopped change erases its stop, and a resume can no longer lift it\"\n    severity: medium\n    priority: p2\n    scope: domain\n    what_happened: >\n      A change blocked on a stop a resume lifts (a stalled specification, an execution error) accepted\n      `/495 pause`. On resume it came back `blocked` with no stop reason, no detail and no longer\n      retryable: a second resume lifted nothing, the names of the lost answers were gone, and cancel\n      was the only way out left.\n    what_expected: >\n      A stopped change keeps its stop, its detail and its ways out whatever the operator does before\n      lifting it.\n    steps_to_reproduce:\n      - \"Take a change to the stop before G0 of a specification that no longer progresses.\"\n      - \"Run `/495